:-) No, ad aquarium is not in UnNetHack.

SporkHack and UnNetHack have quite a different set of special rooms.

I wouldn't call code for special rooms part of the level compiler. In
my view the level compiler is mostly concerned in parsing the
level description files in the dat directory (dat/*.des) and creating
the binary level files needed by the program at runtime.

The level compiler of course needs to know what special rooms there
are if you want to use them in the des files but populating the rooms
is done at runtime while creating a new level for the current game and
the level compiler doesn't have anything to do with that.

